**No.** V4 resolves most of the previous objections as a plan, but its new rule for conflicting source information can put two versions of the same statement into the library, including a version whose source information may be wrong.

For example, in seq 1240, two records quote the same TSMC revenue sentence. One attributes it to the article’s author; the other attributes it to the underlying data set. V4 proposes keeping both if the fields still differ. That preserves the disagreement, but it does not establish which attribution the judge should trust.

## 1. The five round-4 disagreements

| Disagreement | Resolved? | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| **Both meanings and their source information must reach each affected judge** | **Partly — blocker** | V4 now calls for the real writer and both judge requests to be tested with the saved sentence containing **$81.6 billion total revenue** and **$75.2 billion data-center revenue**, including a mutant that drops a summary. That addresses the missing test for the agreeing-attribution case. It does not settle the conflicting-attribution case: v4 keeps both versions without proving which source fields are correct or what the judges receive. [Control-3 result](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/poc/data/parallel-b-link-2026-11-05-v2/gnews_3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32-control-3/result.json>), [v4](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v4.md:10>). |
| **Test each real production entry point** | **Yes, as a plan** | V4 requires replay to be invoked with the split configuration and user defaults, and requires the API and MCP to read the resulting library. The scripts support the narrower conclusion that replay is the ingestion entry point among the three named scripts; the service does not have an ingestion route. The tests still have to be built and pass. [Replay](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/replay.py:51>), [API routes](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/hivemind_api.py:134>), [v4](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v4.md:11>). |
| **Inspect actual judgment reasons for double growth** | **Yes, as a plan** | V4 explicitly re-creates the requests for v79 and v84 with the corrected reference, sends them, reads the reasons, and stops if the judge still counts growth twice. The result remains unproven until that test is done. The saved v79 reason applied 36% growth to an annualized figure that already contained that growth. [Finding and saved reasons](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/r1/claude-findings.md:5>), [v4](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v4.md:12>). |
| **Define the two acceptance measurements and the seeded fixture** | **Partly — serious** | V4 correctly says both measurements are needed, gives a way for the seeded fixture to call the production split and round code, and reserves authorization and thresholds for Alex. But it also says the unseeded run *proves question recall and per-item losses*, then says completeness cannot be proved without a reference. Without a reference, those quantities are limited to what independent readers actually checked. The fixture must also demonstrate that its real round path and initial state are comparable to the control; naming the code alone does not establish comparability. [v4 C-8](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v4.md:16>), [seed refusal](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/replay.py:29>). |
| **Do not automatically prefer B’s attribution** | **Partly — blocker** | V4 removes automatic preference for B and counts actual disagreements. That resolves the original objection to B having automatic authority. The replacement rule—keep both whenever fields differ—introduces the production problem described in section 3. Sharing field definitions is a testable proposal, not proof that either answer will become correct. [v4](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v4.md:13>). |

## 2. V4’s factual claims

- **Judge output: substantially correct, with a limit.** The judge prints one `one_line` and one set of source fields for each evidence record it selects. Therefore, if both summaries are actually preserved inside that one `one_line`, both will be printed. The code does not independently print a summary per original statement or select source fields per summary. Also, it selects evidence before formatting; a link alone does not prove a record appears in every later request. [Judge formatting](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:121>), [evidence selection](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:41>).

- **Entry points: supported within the named scripts.** Replay runs ingestion and writes the library. The API’s only POST route is `/ideas`; the MCP describes itself as a reader. This supports v4’s test arrangement for these entry points, not a claim that no other script anywhere in the repository can write a library. [Replay](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/replay.py:90>), [API](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/hivemind_api.py:134>), [MCP](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/hivemind_mcp.py:1>).

- **16 of 17: verified as a field-difference count.** I grouped matching quotations in `handover.evidence` across the cited trace files, ignoring case and whitespace, and compared speaker, original speaker, original day and tier. There are **17 groups**, of which **16 differ** in at least one of those fields. For example, confirm seq 1211 names the speaker as “Adam Spatacco, reporting CFO Colette Kress’s remarks” versus “fool.com (Adam Spatacco),” while both name Kress as the original speaker. [Seq 1211](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1211.json>).

- **Three substantive differences: observed, but not established as the complete substantive census.** In confirm seq 1240, the original source is “The article’s author, Rafael Müller” versus “The Q2 2026 data set”; in seq 1249 it is “The article’s author” versus “Unspecified source of the market estimate”; in seq 1251 the original day is empty versus `2026-08-30`. Those are the three differences v4 names. Calling the other differences merely convention, or concluding that shared definitions will make them agree correctly, requires source-by-source judgment and the proposed test; the field count alone cannot prove either. [Seq 1240](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1240.json:191>), [seq 1249](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1249.json>), [seq 1251](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1251.json>).

## 3. New blocker or serious problem

**Blocker — keeping both conflicting records does not resolve the conflict and conflicts with the agreed storage rule.** In seq 1240, both versions quote the same sentence: “The same Q2 2026 data set shows that Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing generated NT$1.2 trillion in second-quarter revenue, up 36 percent year over year.” One says the original source was the article’s author; the other says it was the data set. V4’s test requires both to remain separate and flagged, but does not require the incorrect attribution to be corrected before a judge reads it. A flag does not itself make either attribution reliable.

The phase PRD says two items quoting the same sentence are stored as **one record linked to both questions**. The current `sift` also merges identical quotations by retaining the first record and combining links, so v4’s proposed “keep both” is neither the stated PRD behavior nor current behavior. The standard requires the original speaker and meaning to be preserved. This needs a source-faithful resolution and a writer-to-judge test; a change to the PRD’s storage rule would need Alex’s decision. [Seq 1240](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1240.json:191>), [PRD §5.2](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md:107>), [`sift`](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/extraction.py:683>), [standard §5.4](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:408>).

**Serious — the unseeded acceptance claim overstates what it can measure without a reference.** V4 says it proves recall by day and per-item losses, while also acknowledging that completeness needs a reference. A reader checking selected outputs can find errors, but cannot count all missed questions or facts in the window without reading the complete source population against a defined reference. V4 should state the conditional result plainly before acceptance criteria are written. [V4 C-8](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v4.md:27>).

## 4. Agreement

**No, apart from the choices already sent to Alex:**

- **Blocker:** Resolve conflicting source information without storing an unverified duplicate as if it were reliable; prove the result through the real writer and affected judges.
- **Serious:** State that unseeded recall and loss counts require a complete reference, and demonstrate that the seeded comparison uses a comparable real path and starting state.